ollow these safety requirements:)>>endobj1594 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest(G12.1008713)/First 2532 0 R/Last 2533 0 R/Parent 1593 0 R/Title(To shut down electricity to a single lamp:)>>endobj1595 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest(G12.1172286)/First 1596 0 R/Last 1596 0 R/Next 1593 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1597 0 R/Title(Generally, a lamp is replaced after shutting down the entire Atlantium system.)>>endobj1596 0 obj<</Count -5/Dest(G12.1237007)/First 2527 0 R/Last 2528 0 R/Parent 1595 0 R/Title(To shut down the entire system:)>>endobj1597 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1008645)/Next 1595 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1598 0 R/Title(Generally, a lamp is replaced after shutting down the entire Atlantium system. However, in a facility where there is no redundant UV purification, and you require minimizing system downtime, you can replace a lamp while other lamps continue operation...)>>endobj1598 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1172070)/Next 1597 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1599 0 R/Title(When replacing a lamp while the rest of the system is still in operation, you must follow these safety requirements:)>>endobj1599 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1153060)/Next 1598 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1600 0 R/Title(Before commencing this procedure:)>>endobj1600 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1008609)/Next 1599 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1601 0 R/Title(For systems with multiple lamps, the system may continue to operate while any one of the lamps is being replaced, however, precautions must be carried out to protect you from the UV.)>>endobj1601 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1008604)/Next 1600 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1602 0 R/Title(In the Control Module, you can set a margin to assure notification as status declines and a warning is sent to the operator at both the user setting level and the internally coded minimum.)>>endobj1602 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1008600)/Next 1601 0 R/Parent 1416 0 R/Prev 1603 0 R/Title(Each lamp's performance is measured directly by a dedicated UV Intensity Sensor. Replace a lamp when:)>>endobj1603 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1008599)/Next 1