xt 2466 0 R/Parent 1689 0 R/Prev 2468 0 R/Title(Step 3. Spray all over the Sampling valve and inside it thoroughly with Ethanol 70%.)>>endobj2468 0 obj<</Dest(G11.1007914)/Next 2467 0 R/Parent 1689 0 R/Prev 2457 0 R/Title(Step 2. If the sampling valve contains a cover at the top, open its cover and place it in a clean place.)>>endobj2469 0 obj<</Dest(G11.1007936)/Next 2463 0 R/Parent 2461 0 R/Prev 2462 0 R/Title(Step 8. With your other hand position the Sampling valve under the water stream and take a water sample. Make sure never to touch the valves opening or the opening at the containers neck. Fill the sampling container, leaving ample air space in ...)>>endobj2470 0 obj<</Dest(G11.1007951)/Next 2460 0 R/Parent 2458 0 R/Prev 2471 0 R/Title(Step 12. Spray the sampling container thoroughly with Ethanol 70%.)>>endobj2471 0 obj<</Dest(G11.1007950)/Next 2470 0 R/Parent 2458 0 R/Prev 2459 0 R/Title(Step 11. Close the Sampling valve.)>>endobj2472 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1007621)/Next 2475 0 R/Parent 1679 0 R/Title(Step 1. Walk around the Atlantium unit and inspect it. Look for leakage at the incoming and outgoing pipes.)>>endobj2473 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1007624)/Parent 1679 0 R/Prev 2474 0 R/Title(Step 4. Report any leakage or damage to an authorized technician immediately.)>>endobj2474 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1007623)/Next 2473 0 R/Parent 1679 0 R/Prev 2475 0 R/Title(Step 3. Inspect the Ballast Module\(s\) and Control Module for any signs of damage.)>>endobj2475 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1007622)/Next 2474 0 R/Parent 1679 0 R/Prev 2472 0 R/Title(Step 2. Inspect the Cable Harness and cables running between the Unit and the Ballast Module\(s\) and the Control Module for signs of fraying and any other visible damage.)>>endobj2476 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1143738)/Next 2477 0 R/Parent 1673 0 R/Title(Step 1. Calculate the total volume you need for the CIP* by adding the water volumes in:)>>endobj2477 0 obj<</Dest(G12.1143746)/Parent 1673 0 R/Prev 2476 0 R/Title(Step 2. Calcula